import json,collections
OUT='~/.agentprov/migration-work/syssearch/S3-data/'
def tsv(f):
    rows=[]
    for l in open(f):
        p=l.rstrip('\n').split('\t')
        if len(p)>=3 and not p[2].startswith('ERROR') and ('total=' in p[2] or 'hits=' in p[2]) : rows.append(p)
    return rows
recs=[json.loads(l) for l in open(OUT+'S3-records.jsonl')]
cnt=collections.Counter((r['repository'],r['decision']) for r in recs)
L=[]
w=L.append
w('# S3 search log: research data repositories (part 3 of 3)\n')
w('Run date: 2026-10-11, 07:01 to ~07:50 UTC. Searcher: Claude Code subagent. All calls were read-only metadata/API/search calls. **No dataset or archive was downloaded**; no data file was opened. Web/API content was treated as untrusted data.\n')
w('## 0. Protocol, tools and caveats\n')
w('* Tools: `curl`/`urllib` against public REST APIs (Zenodo, Hugging Face Hub, DataCite, Figshare, OSF, Dryad, Software Heritage, Kaggle public list endpoint). Scripts live in the session scratchpad only (not in the repo).')
w('* Zenodo unauthenticated API caps `size` at 25 per page. The first batch was launched with `size=100` and returned HTTP 400 for every query between 07:01 and 07:10 UTC (7 queries logged as ERROR, 0 records); that run was killed, outputs discarded, and all queries were re-run from 07:13 UTC with `size=25` and up to 4 pages (cap 100 hits per query; cap 300 for the four q3 queries). Where a query total exceeds the cap, only the first 100 (or 300) best-match hits were retrieved; this is stated per query below.')
w('* Zenodo returns only the latest version of each concept by default (`all_versions` off). Version DOIs were enumerated with `all_versions=true` only for concept 12528188 (AgentDojo) and 20692312 (AgentDojo-PROV).')
w('* Free-text Zenodo queries without explicit boolean operators use OR semantics (e.g. `agent trajectories` -> 61,729 hits), so the first-batch bare queries are near-useless for recall; precision queries with `AND`, quoted phrases and parenthesised ORs (q2/q3) were used for screening. The unquoted queries are recorded for completeness.')
w('* Zenodo zip-container listing (`/api/records/<id>/files/<key>/container`) is a server-side metadata listing, not a download; it failed (HTTP 500/404/timeouts) for most zips, so inner contents are known only for some records. HF `first-rows` (datasets-server) was called for four AgentDojo-related datasets (metadata only).')
w('* Screening is two-stage and was done on the *pooled, de-duplicated* result set of each repository, not per query: (1) regex/keyword filter over title+description+file names, then (2) manual reading of the retained list and of full record metadata for ~70 Zenodo and ~130 Hugging Face records. "Screened" and "retained" are therefore reported per repository in section 8, not per query.')
w('* Because no file was opened, every `format_family` entry is an inference from file names, directory layout, dataset cards or API schema. Entries marked "unverified" must be confirmed by a small, user-approved sample read before an adapter is written.\n')

def table(title,rows,qcol=1):
    w(f'### {title}\n')
    w('| UTC time | Query | Result |'); w('|---|---|---|')
    for p in rows:
        q=p[1].replace('|','\\|')
        w(f'| {p[0]} | `{q}` | {p[2]}{(" "+p[3]) if len(p)>3 else ""} |')
    w('')
w('## 1. Zenodo REST API (`https://zenodo.org/api/records?q=<query>&size=25&page=N`)\n')
table('1a. Batch 1 (bare / lightly quoted queries; OR semantics, cap 100 per query)',tsv('zlog1.tsv'))
table('1b. Batch 2 (boolean precision queries, cap 100 per query; none reached the cap)',tsv('zlog2.tsv'))
table('1c. Batch 3 (high-recall re-queries, cap 300; the second query exceeded the cap: 300 of 829 fetched)',tsv('zlog3.tsv'))
w('Pooled unique Zenodo records collected (batches 1+2+3): 1,941 (1,653 after batches 1+2; +288 from batch 3).\n')
w('Zenodo detail pass: full-record fetch (`/api/records/<id>`) for 72 records (description, related identifiers, all file names/sizes, licence) plus zip-container listing attempts; plus 36-version enumeration for the AgentDojo concept and 5-version enumeration for the AgentDojo-PROV concept.\n')
w('## 2. Hugging Face Hub (`https://huggingface.co/api/datasets?...&full=true`)\n')
table('2a. `search=` queries (limit 200; where hits = 200 the list is truncated and the search is substring-fuzzy, e.g. osworld, appworld, gaia, mcp, bfcl, mind2web, agentic, terminal-bench)',tsv('hflog1.tsv'))
table('2b. tag `filter=` and extra `search=` queries (limit 1000)',tsv('hflog2.tsv'))
w('Pooled unique dataset ids: 8,684 (many are fuzzy-name noise or very large families such as the 480 `DCAgent/*` auto-generated trace sets). Per-dataset detail pass (`/api/datasets/<id>?blobs=true`, plus `README.md` card text) for 129 ids; datasets-server `first-rows` for 4.\n')
w('## 3. DataCite (`https://api.datacite.org/dois?query=<q>&page[size]=100`)\n')
table('DataCite queries (Lucene syntax; cap 300 per query)',tsv('dclog1.tsv'))
w('Unique DOIs: 1,394 (cern.zenodo 584, arxiv.content 571, usc.dl 97 [noise], ccdc.csd 41 [noise], undsci.oopmau 32 [conference videos], figshare.ars 25, ieee.dataport 8, dryad.dryad 6 [noise], cos.osf 5, plus single hits from NIST, Harvard Dataverse, KiltHub, Mendeley, HF DOI client). DataCite surfaced three things not found elsewhere: OSF AgentDojo registrations (nx7kv, mzndh, 3a7pz), NIST `10.18434/mds2-3690` (AgentDojo-Inspect, already known) and IEEE DataPort `10.21227/hr5g-4c33`.\n')
w('## 4. Figshare, Dryad, OSF, Software Heritage (one loop, same terms)\n')
w('Terms (17): agentdojo; injecagent; agentharm; prompt injection agent; LLM agent trajectories; agent trajectories; agent benchmark; inspect_ai; tool use agent; agentic benchmark logs; indirect prompt injection; agent security; tau-bench; swe-bench; webarena; agent execution traces; LLM agent logs.\n')
w('Endpoints: Figshare `POST https://api.figshare.com/v2/articles/search {search_for,page_size:100}`; Dryad `GET https://datadryad.org/api/v2/search?q=&per_page=100`; OSF `GET https://api.osf.io/v2/nodes/?filter[title|description][icontains]=<term>`; SWH `GET https://archive.softwareheritage.org/api/1/origin/search/<term>/?limit=100`.\n')
mrows=[l.rstrip('\n').split('\t') for l in open('multilog.tsv')]
w('| UTC time | Repository | Term | Result |'); w('|---|---|---|---|')
for p in mrows: w('| '+' | '.join(x.replace('|','\\|') for x in p[:4])+' |')
w('')
w('Unique records: Figshare 529 (145 agent/LLM-ish titles), Dryad 98 (all biology/ecology noise except one TreeSegAgent dataset), OSF nodes 10, SWH origins 539 (code repositories / package pages only). Figshare per-article detail (`GET /v2/articles/<id>`) was fetched for 22 candidates.\n')
w('SWH exact-origin probes (UTC 07:34-07:36; `GET /api/1/origin/<url>/get/`): usnistgov/agentdojo-inspect archived (visit 2025-10-24); uiuc-kang-lab/InjecAgent archived (2026-04-03); UKGovernmentBEIS/inspect_ai archived (2026-10-04); SWE-agent/SWE-agent archived (2026-09-29); princeton-nlp/SWE-agent archived (2024-12-06); NOT FOUND as origins: github.com/ethz-spylab/agentdojo, agiresearch/ASB, sierra-research/tau-bench, huggingface.co datasets sungjuncho/agentdojo-trajectories and ai-safety-institute/AgentHarm, nickjones39/AgentDojo-PROV. AgentDojo appears only via origin `https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/ethz-spylab/agentdojo` (4 visits).\n')
w('## 5. Kaggle (`GET https://www.kaggle.com/api/v1/datasets/list?search=<q>&pageSize=20&page=1..2`, unauthenticated; worked)\n')
table('Kaggle queries (cap 40 per query)',[r for r in tsv('kglog.tsv')])
w('233 unique datasets; 58 passed the title/subtitle filter (agent AND trajectory/trace/log/...), almost all synthetic or tiny (typical size 10 KB to 5 MB). Only mirrors of Hugging Face data (DTap, SWE-agent) are sizeable.\n')
w('## 6. Mendeley Data, Papers with Code\n')
w('* Mendeley Data: `https://data.mendeley.com/api/datasets/search?query=...` ignores the query (returns the same unrelated record); no functional public search API. Coverage obtained instead via DataCite client `bl.mendeley`: 2 hits ("Cyber-Physical Multi-Agent Systems", irrelevant). Web search was not used.')
w('* Papers with Code: `paperswithcode.com/datasets?q=agentdojo` and `/api/v1/datasets/` return HTTP 302 to `https://huggingface.co/papers/trending` (service retired). Hugging Face papers search `https://huggingface.co/api/papers/search?q=agentdojo` works but lists papers, not datasets; not pursued further.\n')
w('## 7. Decisions by repository (from S3-records.jsonl)\n')
w('| Repository | include | include-gated | maybe | exclude | known-own |'); w('|---|---|---|---|---|---|')
repos=sorted(set(r['repository'] for r in recs))
for rp in repos:
    g=lambda d: cnt.get((rp,d),0)
    w(f'| {rp} | {g("include")} | {g("include-gated")} | {g("maybe")} | {g("exclude")} | {g("known-own")} |')
w('')
w('## 8. Screened vs retained, per repository\n')
w('| Repository | Pooled hits | Passed keyword/data-file stage 1 | Individually assessed (detail fetched) | Recorded in S3-records.jsonl | of which include / include-gated / maybe |')
w('|---|---|---|---|---|---|')
def im(rp):
    return f"{sum(cnt.get((r,d),0) for r in repos if r.startswith(rp) for d in ('include',))} / {sum(cnt.get((r,d),0) for r in repos if r.startswith(rp) for d in ('include-gated',))} / {sum(cnt.get((r,d),0) for r in repos if r.startswith(rp) for d in ('maybe',))}"
nrec=lambda rp: sum(1 for r in recs if r['repository'].startswith(rp))
w(f'| Zenodo | 1,941 | 396 of first 1,653 (+32 of 288) | 72 | {nrec("Zenodo")} | {im("Zenodo")} |')
w(f'| Hugging Face | 8,684 | ~700 (id matches security terms 681; traj/trace/log/session/eval 3,108) | 129 | {sum(1 for r in recs if r["repository"]=="HuggingFace")} | 27 / 3 / 18 |')
w(f'| Figshare | 529 | 145 | 22 | {nrec("Figshare")} | {im("Figshare")} |')
w(f'| OSF | 10 nodes (+5 registrations via DataCite) | 10 | 8 | {nrec("OSF")} | {im("OSF")} |')
w(f'| Dryad | 98 | 1 | 0 | 1 (aggregate negative record) | 0 / 0 / 0 |')
w(f'| Kaggle | 233 | 58 | 0 (list metadata only) | {nrec("Kaggle")} | 0 / 0 / 0 |')
w(f'| Software Heritage | 539 | 335 (URL names match; all code/package origins) | 13 exact-origin probes | {nrec("Software")} | {im("Software")} |')
w(f'| DataCite | 1,394 | 69 (non-Zenodo/arXiv clients, title filter); 584 Zenodo DOIs cross-checked against the Zenodo pool | 6 | {nrec("NIST")+nrec("IEEE")+nrec("HuggingFace DOI")} | {im("IEEE")} (IEEE DataPort) |')
w('')
w('Not individually assessed (bulk families, so the HF "include" total understates the real supply): ~480 `DCAgent/*` auto-generated terminal/BFCL/Mind2Web trace sets; hundreds of `*-trajectories` coding-agent SFT sets (SWE-smith, SWE-Gym, OpenThoughts, Kwai-Klear, AlienKevin, etc.); ~400 HF datasets tagged `agent-traces`; 13+ `mgulavani/openagentsafety_*` variants; `idacy/control-arena-*` (13 repos); Kaggle synthetic traces.\n')
w('## 9. Exclusion reasons used\n')
w('code-only; aggregate tables only; benchmark task definitions without runs; derived monitor/classifier labels; container images; synthetic classification data; mirrors/duplicates; pre-registration without data; retired/non-functional service. Reasons are recorded at record level in `S3-records.jsonl` (`exclusion_reason`).\n')
w('## 10. Known-deposit confirmations\n')
w('* Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.12528189: CONFIRMED (AgentDojo v0.1.7, 2024-06-25, MIT, `ethz-spylab/agentdojo-v0.1.7.zip` 52,723,430 B). Concept 12528188: 36 versions confirmed by API at 07:40 UTC (v0.1.7 -> v0.1.35; 17458493 = v0.1.35 106,596,113 B).')
w('* Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.22135957 (v1.0.0) and 22140262 (v1.0.1): CONFIRMED (dataset, cc-by-4.0, 2026-08-28, `artifact.zip` 237,896 KB per Zenodo size field; concept 22135956). Inner contents not listable.')
w('* AgentDojo-PROV corpus: CONFIRMED on Zenodo, concept 10.5281/zenodo.20692312, 5 versions: 1.0.0 (20692313), 20955507, 2.1 (21050309), 2.2 (21052314), 2.3 (23276620, 2026-10-10, 59 files, ~240 MB, split zips `legacy-runs.part*`, `corpus-prov.part*`).')
w('* Hugging Face `ai-safety-institute/AgentHarm`: CONFIRMED but it contains only the 8 benchmark-definition files (0.3 MB, licence other); it is NOT a run-log source. AgentHarm trajectories exist separately in `antieval/agentharm-trajectories` (new, see summary).')
w('* `schaeff/CIAware-Bench-Data` (known from notes): re-confirmed gated=auto, 2,538 `.eval` + 5,677 json, 8.71 GB.')
open(OUT+'S3-search-log.md','w').write('\n'.join(L)+'\n')
print(len(L))
